# Johann Strauss (Sohn), Tritsch-Tratsch-Polka op. 214, the Polka's first strain: the
# pickup and 16 bars, 2/4, A major, the top line of the piano's right hand as printed
# (p. 3; grace notes left out). Bars 2-3 and 10-11 are chords: the top line holds E6
# while an inner voice falls chromatically (D#6 D6 C#6 B5 A5); the song plays them as
# chords, and the check takes their top note. Grid: sixteenths.
source = "Johann Strauss (Sohn), Tritsch-Tratsch-Polka op. 214, Polka, first strain (pickup + 16 bars)"
edition = "First edition, piano, Vienna: Carl Haslinger, plate C.H. 12226, [1858-59], p. 3 (IMSLP #253257)"
steps_per_beat = 4
notes = '''
e5/2 |
e6/2 r/4 e5/2 | e6/2 r/4 e6/2 | e6/2 e6 e6 e6 | e6/2 r/4 f#5/2 |
b5/2 r/4 f#5/2 | b5/2 r/4 g#4/1 a4 | b4/1 c#5 d5 e5 f#5 g#5 a5 b5 | c#6/2 r/4 e5/2 |
e6/2 r/4 e5/2 | e6/2 r/4 e6/2 | e6/2 e6 e6 e6 | e6/2 r/4 g#5/2 |
c#6/2 r/4 g#5/2 | c#6/2 r/4 f#4/1 g#4 | a#4/2 c#5 e5 a#5 | b5/6 b5/2
'''
